{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:8002cc7a9863f282","name":"House Mecetti","source":{"id":"source:reference-8002cc7a9863f282","title":"House Mecetti","revision":24092,"timestamp":"2024-10-20T15:49:09Z","sha256":"10a9a417f1434fa62b9d64a1c11c271e489ba774ccf62a6aa905b9b83258832c","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24092","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=House%20Mecetti&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-8002cc7a9863f282","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy of Intrigue"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_of_Intrigue"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When ",{"tag":"a","children":["Madilon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Madilon","referenceId":"reference:962e80644931660a"}," was discovered on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaan","referenceId":"reference:ffb4373927de3433"},", the floodgates open up to any group interested in capitalizing on the valuable metal. Word spreads as far as ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Tapani Sector"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Tapani_Sector?action=edit&redlink=1"},", and within a few months, parties representing various noble houses of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tapani Nobility"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tapani_Nobility","referenceId":"reference:116393e4f9b4af65"}," arrive in the Luire System, ready join in stripping ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaan","referenceId":"reference:ffb4373927de3433"}," of its assets.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["After ",{"tag":"a","children":["House Reena"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Reena","referenceId":"reference:4016fd407d05a2c5"},", the next of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tapani Nobility"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tapani_Nobility","referenceId":"reference:116393e4f9b4af65"}," to stake a claim on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaan","referenceId":"reference:ffb4373927de3433"}," is House Mecetti. Interested only in what it can gain by exploiting ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaan","referenceId":"reference:ffb4373927de3433"},", House Mecetti chooses to use thinly veiled violence to prey on small-time stakeholders and mining groups. Although House Mecetti's mining operations are plagued by the effects of their poor working conditions, House Mecetti manages to turn a small profit from its activities on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaan","referenceId":"reference:ffb4373927de3433"}," while simultaneously keeping an eye on House Reena's operations.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When the Confederacy invades the Luire System, both ",{"tag":"a","children":["House Reena"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Reena","referenceId":"reference:4016fd407d05a2c5"}," and House Mecetti abstain from taking sides. While ",{"tag":"a","children":["House Reena"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Reena","referenceId":"reference:4016fd407d05a2c5"}," continues to operate at peak capacity, House Mecetti uses the chaos as an opportunity to strengthen its own position through claim jumping operations and outright theft. When the Republic returns, House Mecetti reverts to its covert activities once more.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
